From fa3c61172f1e951cba76212077e50594b758f948 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dameng <dameng@local>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 01:07:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] EDBT v4 B3: cost_c3_greedy priority provider +
 calibration loader + BASELINE line
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Third migration policy for the EDBT v4 baseline matrix. Only the priority
provider differs from our_full/our_freq — candidate set, daemon, byte
budget, strict-fit mapper (B2), copy/publication path, staging, binary and
measurement window are shared:

- cost(s, dev) = sum over gamma in {sequential, monotonic, random, point}
  of calibration(dev, gamma, dtype(s)) x count_gamma(s) x bytes_per_value(s),
  using the RAW cumulative segment-access-counter classes (no EMA,
  documented). benefit(s) = cost(s, CXL) - cost(s, DRAM) feeds the shared
  strict-fit mapper unchanged.
- Dictionary accesses are counted and reported (dictionary_count,
  dictionary_handling=excluded_reported) but excluded from the cost model.
- CLI: --cost_c3_greedy (mutually exclusive with --ablate_d1 and
  --placement_wfreq, enforced) + --c3_calibration <csv> (required).
- Calibration loader verifies the full 2 devices x 4 gammas x 5 dtypes
  grid; local SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4) of the exact file bytes feeds the
  required startup line:
  BASELINE cost_c3_greedy version=<GIT_HEAD_SHA1> calibration_sha256=<sha>
  counter_set=sequential,monotonic,random,point
- Decision trace: c3 rows fill all pattern counters, dictionary handling,
  cost_dram/cost_cxl (total_score = cost_cxl - cost_dram; validator 1e-6);
  semantic columns kept as descriptive fields (rate = raw four-pattern
  total, norm in [0,1]). Trace rows now carry all 50 columns (B1/B2 wrote
  6 empty trailing fields instead of 8 — trailing-empty shortfall only,
  fixed here). Unselected rows with remaining budget > 0 are labeled
  skip_no_fit (strict-fit size skip; unselected => fits_remaining=false
  holds by construction).

Smoke (20s JOB, synthetic calibration): BASELINE line digest equals
sha256sum; 4/4 pattern counters nonzero; per-row recompute of
cost_dram/cost_cxl from counters x calibration x bytes_per_value matches
to 0.0 relative error; max selected bytes per cycle exactly 3,725,884,160
<= budget; zero unselected-but-fits rows.
